{"id": "EUVD-2026-32446", "enisaUuid": "86df24f1-e71b-3e71-89d6-986836a06020", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nibmasm: fix heap over-read in ibmasm_send_i2o_message()\n\nThe ibmasm_send_i2o_message() function uses get_dot_command_size() to\ncompute the byte count for memcpy_toio(), but this value is derived from\nuser-controlled fields in the dot_command_header (command_size: u8,\ndata_size: u16) and is never validated against the actual allocation size.\nA root user can write a small buffer with inflated header fields, causing\nmemcpy_toio() to read up to ~65 KB past the end of the allocation into\nadjacent kernel heap, which is then forwarded to the service processor\nover MMIO.\n\nSilently clamping the copy size is not sufficient: if the header fields\nclaim a larger size than the buffer, the SP receives a dot command whose\nown header is inconsistent with the I2O message length, which can cause\nthe SP to desynchronize. Reject such commands outright by returning\nfailure.\n\nValidate command_size before calling get_mfa_inbound() to avoid leaking\nan I2O message frame: reading INBOUND_QUEUE_PORT dequeues a hardware\nframe from the controller's free pool, and returning without a\ncorresponding set_mfa_inbound() call would permanently exhaust it.\n\nAdditionally, clamp command_size to I2O_COMMAND_SIZE before the\nmemcpy_toio() so the MMIO write stays within the I2O message frame,\nconsistent with the clamping already performed by outgoing_message_size()\nfor the header field.", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:57:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:20:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca1c857e2bb74a9fc0606128334f85316d57067b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b870f652877bfbe321bd0f4096fc37a93296f7b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce57fa439bd1b5d664f334a0c3e3f0e42abb0153", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd19eb1c75047a4ed4e855f56cafd704dc3914e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe31722b0194ff76bf8b461e8bf97a2081147787", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1c2417c60dbdca5ebb00462f21ee71c2d7f7083", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e8f6c9d4ecddda2f28baa1678340286cff3969c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9aad71144fa3682cca3837a06c8623016790e7ec"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4p2m-h7j8-hhxj", "CVE-2026-46064"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05523d18-4bc3-30bf-a8df-0061cf347fbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.86"}, {"id": "065c6d56-4bd1-3dd8-853c-7d9095d5a7dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <ce57fa439bd1b5d664f334a0c3e3f0e42abb0153"}, {"id": "1e70c315-451a-3213-a962-528524cc1882", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.4"}, {"id": "2c3e8f09-068a-38df-801c-83e11166fc25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <9e8f6c9d4ecddda2f28baa1678340286cff3969c"}, {"id": "3759d2d3-9797-31b0-acdb-817c1341c804", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <b870f652877bfbe321bd0f4096fc37a93296f7b6"}, {"id": "3b1a7087-0bcb-3d08-86b1-bb36a0c667e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.258"}, {"id": "3e79b3c4-ef02-3563-8e0a-304d8a4e979a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <ca1c857e2bb74a9fc0606128334f85316d57067b"}, {"id": "49ca392b-e523-3e69-ae9c-944e7a5d0768", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <9aad71144fa3682cca3837a06c8623016790e7ec"}, {"id": "4d5fb323-a0a7-3466-8445-117637033685", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.27"}, {"id": "55d3f673-350d-3724-a30f-a3a7a1f94b4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.209"}, {"id": "5cd1fc74-f7b2-3c53-8069-9dc032e5f6f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "6f2aff62-bd0a-39ea-be1c-73432c82413b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <fe31722b0194ff76bf8b461e8bf97a2081147787"}, {"id": "84effbe3-999e-3323-8efd-d0f34893b3a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c1c2417c60dbdca5ebb00462f21ee71c2d7f7083"}, {"id": "8abe3397-8450-30fe-bcbf-1aefb57a45fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "94054406-fb0b-3a13-b4b6-4b992da1ceea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "99d89fa0-c419-3c6d-911d-42603431d3aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <fd19eb1c75047a4ed4e855f56cafd704dc3914e0"}, {"id": "ae487144-c16e-3f07-be61-75b02c360534", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "ecb5464e-10c2-3a90-8e68-498b44623465", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.140"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c02b3f8e-8e9f-3ada-a045-7dc03c8586b0", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}